====== Linksys NSLU2 ======

{{section>meta:infobox:432_warning#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

{{:media:linksys:nslu2-cover.png?nolink&0x180|}}

The Linksys NSLU2 (a.k.a. SLUG) was a network attached storage device based on the IXP42x processor clocked at 133/266MHz. Is provided with a 2.0A 5V power supply.

**NOTE:** the boardfile support for NSLU2 was deleted along with the rest of IXP4xx from OpenWrt, but was brought back on 2023-05-25 using kernel v6.1 and purely device tree and some rewritten and modernized device drivers. OpenWrt support is under development. You can find preview images of kernel v6.6.x and a working OpenWrt snapshot rootfs with LuCI and KSMBD on [[https://dflund.se/~triad/krad/linksys-nslu2/|this webpage]]. NSLU2 supports only external hard disk or USB boot media as the internal flash is just 8 MB and the flash image will just contain the kernel.
